  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study develops a mixed-integer linear programming model for robust train routing in stations, utilizing absorption graphs to minimize expected delay propagation from primary delays. The approach accounts for both direct and indirect train dependencies as well as dwell-time supplements, and was tested on three railway stations in the Netherlands.",
      "why": "It shifts station routing optimization from simply maximizing buffer times to directly minimizing expected delay propagation, capturing complex, indirect train interactions that traditional buffer-based methods overlook."
